---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Terms of Use and Legal Notice of NZSalary.com" description="Terms of use and legal notice of NZSalary.com: publisher, host, nature of the results, limitation of liability, reuse of content and the free embeddable pay calculator widget." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Terms of use', path: route('terms', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms of use' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Terms of use and legal notice</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>Host</h2>
    <p>Hosting: GitHub Pages, from GitHub, Inc. (San Francisco, CA, USA; street address 88 Colin P Kelly Jr Street, postcode 94107), at <a href={LEGAL.hosting.url} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">pages.github.com</a>. NZSalary.com runs no server of its own: the pages are static files and the PAYE engine is downloaded with them.</p>
    <h2>Nature of the results</h2>
    <p>What you see is a projection of PAYE, ACC earners’ levy, KiwiSaver and student loan deductions for the 2026-27 tax year, using Inland Revenue rates as they stood on the check date shown on each page. Use it to plan, not as financial, tax or legal advice: your payslip, the assessment Inland Revenue issues after the tax year ends on 31 March and a registered tax agent take precedence. Rules the engine does not model are on the <a href={route('method', lang)}>methodology page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Mistakes remain possible despite careful checking, and the site may sometimes be down; reported errors are fixed promptly, but no error-free or uninterrupted service is promised. Choices made on the strength of an estimate are your own responsibility. Where the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 or any other law prevents liability from being limited, these terms do not try to limit it.</p>
    <h2>Reuse</h2>
    <p>You are welcome to quote a sentence or a table row from NZSalary.com if you link to the page it came from; beyond that, the words, tables and source code are under copyright. Embedding the pay calculator is free with the code from the <a href={route('widget', lang)}>widget page</a>, as long as the credit line underneath remains.</p>
    <h2>Applicable law</h2>
    <p>Radif Partners is based in France, so French law applies to these terms. That takes away none of the consumer protections that New Zealand law, or the law where you live, makes compulsory.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
